<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23870" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insĭtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		1. insero. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An ingrafting</i>, <i>grafting</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec consitiones modo delectant, sed etiam
					insitiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Sen. 15, 54</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 3, 9, 6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That which is ingrafted</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insitionem nutrire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 5, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. Arb. 8,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The time of grafting</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am. 195</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
